# Simple English for engineer-facing writing: always apply

Before you write or rewrite any of these, read and apply
[`simple-english`](../skills/simple-english/SKILL.md):

- A pull request body, title, or commit message.
- A review comment, a review summary, or a reply to review feedback.
- A ticket summary, description, or comment.
- A chat message to an engineer about work in this codebase.
- A written answer to an engineer about work in this codebase.

It does not bind code, identifiers, commands, file paths, quoted error text, or customer-facing
marketing copy.

## Forbidden

- Cutting a hedge to reach a word count. The modal rule governs requirement strength, never
  confidence.
- Dropping a safety condition, an exception, or a scope qualifier to reach a word count.
